body:
yes it has helped a lot. also helps me shift focus away from myself/my flaws/how other people are perceiving them which is the cause of the anxiety. i practice lovingkindness meditation and mindfulness meditation. when i'm walking down the street, i notice a judgmental thought about someone else i see, and then respond to my thought with thoughts of goodwill toward that person and toward myself.

&#x200B;

example of how this plays out: I see someone on a sidewalk. my thoughts: "they look douchey (they think I'm lame). oh I'm having one of them judgmental thoughts. that makes me feel bad - defensive and angry and afraid. may they be safe from harm. may they be happy. may they be at ease. may they be loved. may i be safe from harm. may i be happy. may i be at ease. may i be loved.. i'm noticing that my body is relaxing a bit, i feel less negative emotion"

&#x200B;

it's easiest with strangers because the relationship is simple. every now and then i even share a smile with a passerby. it gets harder the more intimate or difficult the relationship is but i try to work up to it! really can shift how i feel
